#!/usr/bin/python3
# System Python on purpose: `env python3` can resolve to a mise shim, which adds the mise exec
# env (CARGO_HOME, RUSTUP_*). hcom treats CARGO_* as a contaminated parent and replaces the
# PATH of launched agents with one rebuilt from a clean login shell (no mise shims).
"""hcom-gui: catalog agents and live instances in one table, with buttons that run hcom.

The GUI holds no hcom logic: the table comes from `hcom agent list --all --json` and
`hcom list --json`; every button runs an existing command and logs its output.

Optional ~/.hcom/gui.json:
  {"refresh_seconds": 5,
   "open_with": [{"label": "Zed", "cmd": ["zed", "{dir}"], "key": "z"},
                 {"label": "gitg", "cmd": ["gitg"], "cwd": "{dir}"},
                 {"label": "Backlog", "cmd": ["x-terminal-emulator", "backlog", "board"], "cwd": "{dir}",
                  "if_exists": "{dir}/backlog"}],
   "commands": [{"label": "Kill persistent", "cmd": ["hcom", "kill", "@persistent"], "confirm": true}],
   "columns": ["agent", "instance", "status", "context", "git"],
   "attach": {"herdr": ["sh", "-c", "hcom agent attach \"$1\" && wmctrl -x -a herdr.herdr", "_", "{instance}"]}}
"attach" maps the terminal an instance runs in (Where column) to the Attach command;
other terminals run DEFAULT_ATTACH.
"commands" run as written, without a selected row (optional: confirm, cwd, key).
"key" (any button) is a Tk event sequence bound in the table, e.g. "z" or "<F2>", shown
in the button label ("Zed (z)").
"open_with" programs also start while an hcom command runs; a quick non-zero exit is logged.
"stats_seconds" (default 60) is how often the usage columns reload life and message events.
"idle_seconds" (default 10): once an instance has been listening this long, the Idle column gets
its class from contrib/idle-classifier/idle_check.py (needs_user, waiting, done; "-" none), once per
listening period. Remote instances report no listening age: they count from the GUI's first sight.
A needs_user row is highlighted in blue, less loudly than a blocked one. Right-click on a classified
row corrects its class (idle_check.py --label, shown with ✓).
"columns" selects and orders the table columns (keys of COLUMNS; default: all); a choice
made with the Columns… button is kept in gui-state.json and takes precedence (Reset drops it);
a column added to hcom-gui after that choice is shown in its default place.
Heading clicks cycle the sort: ascending, descending, default. The Filter field matches
agent, instance, dir and groups (case-insensitive).
A disabled catalog agent's row is struck through; Hide disabled (on by default) hides it.
Hide non-persistent hides instances without a catalog agent. The window title counts the shown rows.
Start: the empty Name field gets "<agent>__" on focus; left unchanged it counts as empty.
Window layout, columns, sort and filters (Running only, Blocked only, Hide disabled, Hide
non-persistent) are kept in ~/.hcom/gui-state.json.
"""

